      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Religious conservatives typically argue that medical aid in dying violates the sanctity of life and the right to natural death, often citing the belief that only God has the authority to determine the end of a life. In contrast, religious liberals often embrace the right to autonomy and dignity in the face of suffering, arguing that the mere promise of a good life is an illusion and that the state should recognize the inherent right to end one's own suffering. These opposing core logics generally hinge on the tension between protecting the sanctity of biological life versus affirming the moral agency and suffering of the individual.",
